# What `docker build` may see. The Dockerfile COPYs an explicit whitelist, so
# this is defence in depth plus a small build context.
#
# Docker's matcher does NOT cross `/`, so a bare `*` with `!name` negations
# works here. .gcloudignore next door uses gitignore semantics and needs
# leading slashes instead — the two files are not interchangeable.
*

!pyproject.toml
!poetry.lock
!airglider
!app
!clients
!common
!config
!db

# never bake real secrets into the image (re-excluded after !config above)
config/.env
config/.env.*

# SQL run against the database, never read by the app: db/init builds a fresh
# database, db/commands holds ad-hoc queries and dated migrations
db/init
db/commands

**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
